vendor/bundle/
.bundle/
Gemfile.lock

# Certificates (never commit)
*.p12
*.cer
*.mobileprovision

# The snapshot gate's record switch: its presence turns the suite from checking
# the recorded goldens into overwriting them, so it is a file to create for one
# run and delete — never to commit. `Tools/assert-snapshot-gate.py` fails while
# it exists in a checkout, which is the backstop for forgetting.
.snapshot-record

# Snapshot diff-gate failures: the recorded image, the rendered one and the
# overlay between them, written by a failing run for somebody to look at. CI
# uploads them as an artifact; a committed `actual.png` beside the goldens is
# how one of them gets mistaken for the other. See docs/snapshot-testing.md.
SnapshotFailures/

# The UI test host's Xcode project, generated from `UITestHost/project.yml` by
# `xcodegen generate`. A `project.pbxproj` is machine-written plist keyed by
# opaque UUIDs: nobody reviews a diff in one, Xcode rewrites parts of it on
# open, and two branches that both touch it conflict unresolvably. The spec is
# the reviewable artefact and this is its output. See `docs/ui-testing.md`.
UITestHost/*.xcodeproj
UITestHost/*.xcworkspace
UITestHost/UITestResults.xcresult

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.log
test-output/
TestResults.xcresult

# Python bytecode from the audit scripts in Tools/ and .github/scripts/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
